/T (complex enterprise requirements, namely performance and scalability, complex business logic, system integration, customisation, security and governance, AI and advanced technology, vendor or platform dependency, and data management. It also showed how a hybrid low-code/pro-code approach can address requirements beyond standard low-code capabilities.)
/E (complex enterprise requirements, namely performance and scalability, complex business logic, system integration, customisation, security and governance, AI and advanced technology, vendor or platform dependency, and data management. It also showed how a hybrid low-code/pro-code approach can address requirements beyond standard low-code capabilities.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [22]
>>
