566 0 obj
<<
/Title (develop the standard parts of the system rapidly: forms for job applications and applicant details, reports on application history, workflows for application processing and HR approval, notifications, and basic dashboards. These features correspond to the capabilities that low-code platforms are designed to provide.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 478 0 R
/Next 567 0 R
>>
endobj
567 0 obj
<<
/Title (As the organisation grows, the requirements become more demanding. A large number of applicants, applications and records raises performance and data-management concerns; integration with CRM, HRMS and job portals raises integration concerns; differing access needs and the handling of applicant personal data raise security and governance concerns; and advanced features such as intelligent resume screening may need external services. In such cases, extensions, integrations or custom development may be needed in addition to the low-code application. Low-code is therefore useful for rapidly developing standard business applications, whereas increasingly complex enterprise requirements may call for a hybrid approach, and the choice should be based on the requirements of the application.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 478 0 R
/Prev 566 0 R
>>
endobj
568 0 obj
<<
/Title (Thecase study demonstrated the major limitations that can arise when low-code platforms are applied to)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 479 0 R
/Next 569 0 R
>>
endobj
569 0 obj
<<
/Title (complex enterprise requirements, namely performance and scalability, complex business logic, system integration, customisation, security and governance, AI and advanced technology, vendor or platform dependency, and data management. It also showed how a hybrid low-code/pro-code approach can address requirements beyond standard low-code capabilities.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 479 0 R
/Prev 568 0 R
>>
endobj
570 0 obj
<<
/Title (become more significant as enterprise complexity increases. For an application such as the Enterprise Job Application Management System, standard functionality can be built quickly using low-code, while demanding requirements in logic, integration, security, scale and advanced technology may need pro-code extensions. It is therefore important to understand the limitations of a platform before selecting a development approach, so that the chosen approach matches the requirements of the enterprise application.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 410 0 R
/Prev 480 0 R
/Next 481 0 R
>>
endobj
